This project focuses on the design and installation of the electronic system for a campervan, aiming to create a self-sufficient and comfortable mobile home. It integrates control, monitoring, and safety systems while optimizing energy consumption through solar power and efficient electrical planning.
🎯 Project Goals

    Install and configure a control panel to monitor and manage:

        Lighting

        Clean and grey water levels

        Battery status

    Implement a door alarm system and additional CCTV cameras for security.

    Calculate daily energy consumption of appliances to determine the required battery capacity.

    Integrate solar panels and ensure proper installation of electrical protections such as circuit breakers and residual current devices.

    Ensure the entire system complies with low voltage safety regulations (BOE).

🛠️ Features & Scope

    Energy Management: Estimation of power usage and battery sizing for full autonomy.

    Solar Energy Integration: Planning and theoretical mounting of solar panels.

    Space Optimization: Efficient arrangement of electronic components within the campervan.

    Security & Monitoring: Alarm system and optional CCTV integration.

    Regulatory Compliance: Study and application of electrical safety standards for homologation.

🧭 Motivation

This project stems from a lifelong passion for campervans and the desire to build one step by step. Inspired by the self-sufficiency of animals like turtles and snails, the goal is to create a mobile home that offers:

    Flexibility: Travel and adapt to different environments without restrictions.

    Comfort: Enjoy modern amenities—hot coffee, warm showers, silent nights—anywhere.

    Independence: Live, study, and work from any location while staying off-grid.

📚 Learning Outcomes

Through this project, I aim to:

    Deepen my understanding of electronics, solar energy, and low-voltage regulations.

    Master the practical aspects of designing and installing electrical systems.

    Gain hands-on experience balancing cost, efficiency, and safety.

🔧 Technologies & Components

    Solar Panels – energy harvesting and integration

    Batteries – sizing and energy storage management

    Control Panel – real-time monitoring and control

    Alarm System & CCTV – enhanced safety features

    Electrical Protections – circuit breakers and differential switches

✨ This project is a step toward merging passion, sustainability, and engineering—turning a dream of a mobile home into a functional reality.
